  {
   "id": "l-tener-hay",
   "title": "tener and hay",
   "summary": "Having, ages, feelings, and \"there is / there are\".",
   "cards": [
    {
     "rule": "**tengo, tienes, tiene, tenemos, tenéis, tienen.** Spanish uses *tener* for age and feelings: **tengo 30 años, tengo hambre / sed / frío / calor / sueño**. **tener que** + infinitive = must.",
     "examples": [
      {
       "id": "s-tengo-anos",
       "es": "Tengo treinta años.",
       "en": "I am thirty years old."
      },
      {
       "id": "s-tenemos-frio",
       "es": "Tenemos frío.",
       "en": "We are cold."
      },
      {
       "id": "s-tienen-que",
       "es": "Tienen que trabajar.",
       "en": "They have to work."
      }
     ],
     "trap": "Never *Soy hambriento*: hunger, thirst and age are things you *have*."
    },
    {
     "rule": "**hay** = there is / there are (one form for both). Use **hay** for something new, **está / están** for something already known.",
     "examples": [
      {
       "id": "s-hay-banco",
       "es": "Hay un banco cerca.",
       "en": "There is a bank nearby."
      },
      {
       "id": "s-donde-esta-banco",
       "es": "¿Dónde está el banco?",
       "en": "Where is the bank?"
      },
      {
       "id": "s-no-hay-problema",
       "es": "No hay problema.",
       "en": "No problem."
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
