   "id": "l-questions",
   "title": "Negation and questions",
   "summary": "Put no before the verb. Question words always take an accent.",
   "cards": [
    {
     "rule": "Negative: **no** before the verb. Double negatives are correct: **No tengo nada. No hablo con nadie.** Yes/no question: same words, raised voice, and **¿ ?**.",
     "examples": [
      {
       "id": "s-no-hablo",
       "es": "No hablo inglés.",
       "en": "I don't speak English."
      },
      {
       "id": "s-no-tengo-nada",
       "es": "No tengo nada.",
       "en": "I have nothing."
      },
      {
       "id": "s-hablas-espanol",
       "es": "¿Hablas español?",
       "en": "Do you speak Spanish?"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "rule": "**¿qué?** what · **¿quién?** who · **¿dónde?** where · **¿cuándo?** when · **¿cómo?** how · **¿por qué?** why (**porque** = because) · **¿cuánto?** how much · **¿cuál?** which.",
     "examples": [
      {
       "id": "s-como-te-llamas",
